          "text": "Yes, clipless pedals are worth considering for a mountain bike, even for casual riders. They provide several advantages, such as improved power transfer, better foot stability, and increased control over rough terrain. With your preference for comfort over speed, clipless pedals can enhance your riding experience by keeping your feet securely attached to the pedals, which helps maintain a consistent pedal stroke and reduces fatigue on longer rides. If you choose to go this route, consider pedals with a dual-platform design, allowing you to use regular shoes when necessary, which can be beneficial for casual riding and walking.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0028-49-15457:0": 0.44717302918434143,
            "clueweb22-en0036-51-05870:13": 0.3329653739929199,
            "clueweb22-en0000-09-06499:4": 0.29486164450645447,
            "clueweb22-en0036-51-05870:12": 0.18930253386497498,
            "clueweb22-en0045-51-14333:0": 0.07751710712909698,
            "clueweb22-en0038-75-04839:0": 0.06509101390838623,
