    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! Considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats?",
          "user_rubrik": "Considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Given your history of back pain, selecting a bicycle seat with features that prioritize comfort and support is essential. Look for saddles with ergonomic designs, such as those with a center cut-out or relief channel, which help reduce pressure on sensitive areas and improve weight distribution. Padded seats with gel or foam cushioning can also absorb shocks and vibrations, especially on rough terrain. Additionally, consider seats with elastomer dampers or suspension systems to further minimize impact. Wide saddles with a contoured shape can provide better support for your sit bones, reducing strain on your lower back. Adjustable seat angles and heights are also important to ensure proper posture while riding, which can alleviate back discomfort. Brands like Bikeroo and Planet Bike offer options tailored for comfort and back support, making them worth exploring.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0043-33-03891:8": 26.168399810791016,
