    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Actually, considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats?",
          "user_rubrik": "Considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "If you have a history of back pain, selecting a comfortable, supportive saddle is crucial. Look for a saddle with ample padding and a width that matches your sit bones, as this helps distribute your weight evenly and reduces pressure on your lower back [clueweb22-en0016-81-08821:7][clueweb22-en0001-79-06259:2]. The angle and position of the saddle are also important: a saddle that is tilted too far up or down can contribute to back pain, so keeping it level is recommended [clueweb22-en0002-61-12317:0]. Features like gel or foam cushioning, and possibly a pressure-relief channel, can further enhance comfort, especially for casual riders on rough terrain [clueweb22-en0036-82-10766:6]. If you continue to experience discomfort, a professional bike fitting can help you find the optimal saddle and position for your needs. Would you like tips on adjusting your saddle position for back comfort?",
