    "topic": "9-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Are clipless pedals ever worth considering for mountain biking if you mostly do casual riding and comfort is your main goal?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Clipless pedals (which require special shoes that attach to the pedal) provide better pedaling efficiency and can make climbing hills less strenuous, but they are generally favored by riders seeking performance or riding on technical terrain [clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:4]. For casual riders who value comfort and want to use regular shoes, flat pedals are recommended because they allow quick foot placement and removal, which is especially helpful on rough or muddy trails [clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:4]. If you're curious about trying clipless pedals, there are hybrid or dual-platform pedals that let you use either regular shoes or cycling shoes with cleats, offering flexibility for different situations [clueweb22-en0036-51-05870:13]. However, for most comfort-oriented, non-competitive riders, flat pedals with good grip are the best choice. Would you like recommendations for specific flat pedals with excellent grip?",
