            "clueweb22-en0004-51-01356:1": 0.05499957741892845
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I value comfort over speed.",
            "I care about sustainability and avoiding waste.",
            "I'm a casual bike rider.",
            "I recently moved to a city with more hills and rough paths.",
            "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Actually, are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike? I\u2019m a bit unsure if they\u2019d suit me as a casual rider.",
          "user_rubrik": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Clipless pedals attach your feet to the pedals, improving efficiency and making uphill climbs easier, which can be beneficial for mountain biking. However, they require special shoes and can feel restrictive, especially for casual riders who may need to put a foot down quickly on rough trails. Platform pedals, on the other hand, allow you to use any shoes and make it easier to get on and off the bike, which many casual and comfort-focused riders prefer. Hybrid or dual-platform pedals combine both systems, letting you ride clipped in or with regular shoes, offering flexibility if you want to try clipless without fully committing. If comfort, ease of use, and versatility are your priorities, platform or hybrid pedals are likely the best choice for you as a casual rider [clueweb22-en0036-51-05870:13][clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:4][clueweb22-en0017-66-09315:12]. Would you like recommendations for specific platform or hybrid pedals?",
