    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks! Actually, considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats?",
          "user_rubrik": "Considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To minimize back pain while riding, look for a bike seat that is extra wide and ergonomically designed to distribute pressure evenly and relieve strain on your lower back and tailbone. Features such as dual spring or rubber ball shock absorbers help cushion bumps on rough terrain, reducing the impact transmitted to your spine [clueweb22-en0006-11-01516:1][clueweb22-en0018-97-08854:5]. High-density memory foam or gel padding further enhances comfort by molding to your body and supporting your sit bones. It's also important to ensure the saddle is properly adjusted to your height and riding position, as this helps maintain an ergonomic posture and reduces back strain [clueweb22-en0026-98-04247:9]. Would you like recommendations for specific saddle brands or models?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0006-11-01516:1": 0.05527755195466349,
