    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes a lot of sense\u2014thanks! Moving on, what are the key things to look for on mountain bike pedals?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the key things to look for on mountain bike pedals?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When choosing mountain bike pedals, look for lightweight construction and sealed bearings to keep out dirt and moisture, which extends pedal life and reduces maintenance needs [clueweb22-en0041-01-01966:1][clueweb22-en0004-51-01356:2]. Platform pedals made from durable nylon fiber or aluminum alloy with anti-slip surfaces and strategically placed pins offer excellent grip and comfort, especially for casual riders who value comfort over speed [clueweb22-en0043-57-01365:10]. These pedals are easy to use with any footwear and are suitable for both city and forest trail riding. Some recommended models include the Puroma Mountain Bike Pedal (nylon fiber, non-slip), FOOKER MTB Pedals (nylon fiber, anti-slip studs), and Crankbrothers Stamp (adjustable grip, minimal profile) [clueweb22-en0004-51-01356:1]. Choosing quality pedals with these features supports sustainability by reducing the need for frequent replacements. Would you like tips on maintaining your pedals for longevity?",
