      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, helpful points! What saddle types would you recommend for comfort on rough trails?",
          "user_rubrik": "What types of saddles are recommended for a mountain bike used primarily on forest trails and rough bike paths?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For maximum comfort on rough trails as a casual, sustainability-minded rider, prioritize these saddle features and models:\n\n**Top Recommendation:**  \n- **Wide, well-padded saddles with suspension** are best for comfort and shock absorption on bumpy paths.  \n- **Gel or dual-density foam padding** offers plush support, but foam lasts longer and resists compacting\u2014ideal for sustainability and less frequent replacement.  \n- **Sprung or elastomer suspension** under the saddle further smooths rough terrain.\n\n**Specific Models Frequently Recommended:**  \n- **Sunlite Cloud-9**: Extra-wide, dual-density foam + gel, built-in springs. Highly rated for comfort and durability, fits most bikes, ideal for casual and recreational use.\n- **Bikeroo Oversized Comfort Saddle**: Wide, plush, with elastomer or steel springs. Universally compatible, waterproof, and praised for comfort on city and trail rides.\n- **Brooks B17**: Leather, firmer but molds to you over time\u2014very durable and sustainable, but requires a break-in period.\n\n**Fit Matters",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0016-88-10248:13": -0.009991866536438465,
            "clueweb22-en0016-88-10248:12": -0.010056187398731709,
