          "user_utterance": "That sounds useful! What should I consider when selecting new tires for my bike?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For comfort, sustainability, and minimal hassle on hilly, rough city paths, here\u2019s what matters most when choosing new bike tires:\n\n**1. Tire Width & Comfort**\n- Go wider: 28\u201332mm (for hybrids/commuters) or 2.0\u20132.4\" (for mountain/comfort bikes) cushions bumps and improves grip\u2014ideal for rough paths and casual riding ([clueweb22-en0046-36-11753], [clueweb22-en0006-47-03454]).\n- Check your bike\u2019s frame/brake clearance before upsizing ([clueweb22-en0016-81-17420]).\n\n**2. Tread Pattern**\n- Light or semi-slick tread: Smooth center with light side knobs balances comfort, grip, and easy rolling on mixed surfaces ([clueweb22-en0046-36-11753], [clueweb22-en0016-81-17420]).\n- Avoid aggressive knobby treads unless you ride mostly off-road\u2014they add rolling resistance and effort ([clueweb22",
