          "user_utterance": "Thanks for the advice! What about tire pressure\u2014how do I know the right pressure for my bike?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For comfort, safety, and sustainability on rough, hilly city rides, here\u2019s how to find the right tire pressure\u2014without getting lost in technicalities:\n\n**1. Start With the Sidewall:**  \n- Your tire\u2019s sidewall lists a pressure range (e.g., 40\u201365 psi). Stay within this.\n\n**2. Go Lower for Comfort:**  \n- Wider tires (e.g., 32\u201340mm or 2.0\u20132.4\") work best at lower pressures\u2014think 30\u201350 psi for hybrids, 30\u201340 psi for gravel/MTB ([clueweb22-en0010-15-16096], [clueweb22-en0008-23-06738]).\n- Lower pressure = more shock absorption and grip, ideal for rough paths and rain.\n\n**3. Adjust for Weight:**  \n- Heavier riders need slightly higher pressure; lighter riders can go lower ([clueweb22-en0008-23-06738], [clueweb22-en0043-23-02933]).\n\n**4",
