          "user_utterance": "Those are great tips! What should I consider when choosing grips or tape for the handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the key things to look for on mountain bike pedals?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For comfort-focused, sustainable handlebar upgrades\u2014especially for rough, hilly city rides\u2014prioritize these essentials:\n\n**1. Grips vs. Tape:**\n- **Flat bars (most city/hybrid/MTB bikes):** Go for ergonomic grips.\n- **Drop bars (road bikes):** Use padded handlebar tape.\n\n**2. What to Look For:**\n- **Ergonomics:** Winged or contoured grips (like Ergon GP1/GA3) reduce hand pain and numbness\u2014ideal for casual riders and rough paths.\n- **Padding:** Extra gel or foam absorbs shocks. Thicker grips/tape (e.g., Lizard Skins 3.2mm, Ergon GA2 Fat) are best for comfort.\n- **Grip/Traction:** Textured, tacky surfaces prevent slipping, even in rain or without gloves.\n- **Lock-on Design:** Prevents twisting and is easy for a shop to install\u2014no DIY hassle.\n- **Sustainable Materials:** Cork or natural rubber options (like Asti cork grips) are",
