          "text": "When it comes to a second-hand bike, safety and comfort are crucial. First, inspect the brakes, as they are essential for safety. Check if they are functioning properly and consider upgrading them if necessary. Next, look at the saddle and adjust it to a comfortable height to ensure you can touch the floor with both feet. Additionally, check the tires for wear and consider replacing them",
