          "text": "For a mountain bike used on forest trails and rough bike paths, consider handlebars that provide a comfortable riding position and allow for easy control. Riser bars can be a good option as they facilitate a more upright posture, which can help reduce strain on your back. Additionally, look for handlebars with a comfortable width and a grip that provides adequate traction and comfort. Some handlebars also feature a unique shape or design, such as a flare or sweep, which can help improve control and reduce fatigue on long rides. Ultimately, the best handlebars for you will depend on your personal preferences and riding style, so it's a good idea to try out different options to see what works best for you.",
