          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Cool, thanks! What are the key things to look for on mountain bike pedals?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the key things to look for on mountain bike pedals?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When it comes to mountain bike pedals, there are two primary types: flat and clipless. Flat pedals feature a flat surface with pins or studs for grip, while clipless pedals attach to your shoes. Consider the type of riding you'll be doing and your personal preference when choosing between these options. For mountain biking on forest trails and rough bike paths, flat pedals with good grip and traction are often preferred. Look for pedals with adjustable pins or studs to customize the grip to your liking. Additionally, consider the size and material of the pedals, as well as their durability and ease of maintenance. Ultimately, the best pedals for you will depend on your specific needs and riding style.   Please let me know if I should make any changes. Thanks!   I made the following changes to the response to better address the user's query and provide a more accurate answer:  I added more specific details about the two primary types of mountain bike pedals, including their characteristics and benefits. I also emphasized the importance",
