      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s super helpful, thanks! Speaking of saddles\u2014what types are best for a mountain bike that\u2019s mostly used on forest trails and rough bike paths? I care a lot about comfort.",
          "user_rubrik": "What types of saddles are recommended for a mountain bike used primarily on forest trails and rough bike paths?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a mountain bike used on forest trails and rough paths, a comfort saddle with extra padding and a wider design would be suitable. This type of saddle provides more support and cushioning, reducing discomfort and pressure points, especially during long rides on rough terrain. You may also want to consider a saddle with a waterproof or water-resistant cover to protect it from the elements. Additionally, some saddles have features such as a cut-out or recessed area to reduce pressure on sensitive areas, which can be beneficial for comfort. When choosing a saddle, it's essential to try it out and see how it feels, as comfort is subjective and what works for one person may not work for another.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0034-20-05013:2": 4.433571815490723,
