          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, considering your history of back pain, it's essential to look for a bicycle seat that provides adequate support and comfort. A seat with extra padding, a wider design, and a cut-out or recessed area to reduce pressure on sensitive areas can help alleviate discomfort. Additionally, a seat with a ergonomic design that supports your hips and allows your legs to move freely can also help reduce strain on your back. You may also want to consider a seat with a suspension system to absorb bumps and shocks, which can help reduce the impact on your back. It's crucial to try out different seats to find the one that works best for you and provides the necessary comfort and support.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.   (I made the changes as per the critique, I removed the last two sentences and made the answer more concise)   Considering your history of back pain, look for a bicycle seat with extra padding, a wider design, and a cut-out or recessed area to",
