      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense, thanks. Could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik": "Could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a mountain bike used on forest trails and rough paths, consider handlebars with a more upright position and a wider design to provide more control and comfort. You may also want to look into handlebars with a slight backsweep or rise, which can help reduce strain on your back and wrists. Additionally, ergonomic handlebar grips can provide extra comfort and support for your hands during long rides. These features can help improve your overall riding experience and reduce discomfort.",
