      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s clear. Now, what are the key things to look for on mountain bike pedals?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the key things to look for on mountain bike pedals?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When looking for mountain bike pedals, consider the material quality, grip, and type of pedal. Flat pedals with pins or studs provide good grip, while clipless pedals offer a secure connection to your shoes. The material should be durable and lightweight, such as aluminum alloys. Additionally, consider the size of the pedal and the level of adjustability to ensure a comfortable fit. If you prioritize comfort and control, look for pedals with a wide platform and adjustable pins or studs. It's also essential to consider your riding style and the type of terrain you'll be riding on to choose the most suitable pedal type.",
