          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Clipless pedals can be beneficial for mountain biking, especially for long durations and efficient pedaling. They provide a secure connection to your shoes, allowing for better pedal efficiency and power transfer. However, they may require some time to adjust to, and clipping in and out can be slower than with flat pedals. If you prioritize comfort and control, you may want to consider hybrid or dual-platform pedals that offer the flexibility of a flat pedal on one side and a clipless system on the other. This can provide the best of both worlds, especially for casual riders who value comfort over speed. Ultimately, it depends on your personal preference and riding style.",
