          "text": "For a mountain bike used primarily on forest trails and rough bike paths, I would recommend a saddle with sufficient padding for your sit bones. A saddle with a long-lasting cover and an aerodynamic shape would also be beneficial for efficient movements. Additionally, consider a saddle that is designed specifically for mountain biking, as these tend to have more padding and a wider nose to provide better support and comfort. This type of saddle will help you to make efficient movements and provide the necessary comfort for your ride. Choose a saddle that has a long-lasting cover to ensure it can withstand the rough terrain and harsh weather conditions. This will help you to enjoy your ride without any discomfort or pain. Choose a saddle that is designed specifically for mountain biking to ensure you get the best comfort and support for your ride. Consider a saddle with a cut-out or a recessed area to reduce pressure on sensitive areas. This will help to prevent discomfort and pain during long rides. Consider a saddle with a suspension system to absorb shock and vibrations",
