          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s really useful, thanks! Considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats?",
          "user_rubrik": "Considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, when it comes to bicycle seats, there are several features to consider, especially if you have a history of back pain. A saddle with sufficient padding for your sit bones is essential to provide comfort and support. Look for a saddle with a long-lasting cover and an aerodynamic shape to help you move efficiently. A saddle designed specifically for mountain biking, with more padding and a wider nose, can provide better support and comfort. Additionally, consider a saddle with a cut-out or a recessed area to reduce pressure on sensitive areas, which can help prevent discomfort and pain during long rides. A saddle with a suspension system can also help absorb shock and vibrations, making your ride more comfortable. It's also a good idea to consider a saddle with a shock-absorbing feature, which can help dampen road shocks and bumps. This can be especially helpful if you're riding on rough terrain or uneven surfaces. By considering these features, you can find a saddle that provides the necessary comfort and support for",
