      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful! Now, about pedals\u2014what are the key things to look for on mountain bike pedals?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the key things to look for on mountain bike pedals?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When it comes to mountain bike pedals, there are several key things to look for. First, consider the type of riding you'll be doing most often. If you'll be riding on technical trails or steep terrain, you may want to look for pedals with a more aggressive design and a wider platform. This will provide better support and stability for your feet. Additionally, look for pedals with a durable material, such as aluminum or steel, and a design that allows for easy clip-in and clip-out. Consider pedals with a platform size that fits your foot size, as this will provide better support and comfort. You may also want to look for pedals with a adjustable float, which will allow you to customize the amount of movement in your foot. Finally, consider the type of cleat system you prefer, such as SPD or clipless. By considering these features, you can find pedals that provide the necessary support and comfort for your ride. It's also a good idea to consider the weight and durability of",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0014-28-02436:12": 0.88163822889328,
