        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense. Speaking of comfort, what types of saddles are recommended for a mountain bike used primarily on forest trails and rough bike paths?",
          "user_rubrik": "What types of saddles are recommended for a mountain bike used primarily on forest trails and rough bike paths?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a mountain bike used primarily on forest trails and rough bike paths, I would recommend a saddle with a lot of cushioning and a cutout or hole in the middle. This type of saddle is designed to reduce pressure on the perineal area and provide extra comfort on rough terrain. Additionally, a saddle with a slightly wider shape can also provide more support and comfort for long rides. Look for a saddle with a durable material, such as leather or synthetic leather, and a design that allows for good airflow to prevent overheating. Some popular types of saddles for mountain biking include gel saddles, suspension saddles, and saddles with a lot of padding. It's also a good idea to try out different saddles before making a purchase to find the one that feels most comfortable for you.  (",
