          "text": "Considering your history of back pain, I would recommend looking for a bicycle seat with a cutout or hole in the middle. This design can help reduce pressure on the perineal area and alleviate discomfort. Additionally, a seat with a lot of cushioning and a slightly wider shape can provide extra support and comfort for your back. You may also want to consider a seat with a suspension system, which can help absorb shock and vibrations from the road, reducing strain on your back. It's also a good idea to try out different seats before making a purchase to find the one that feels most comfortable for you.  Answer should be less than 200 words.  Please let me know if you need any further clarification.  Thank you.  I will be happy to answer any follow-up questions.  Please go ahead and ask your next question.  I am here to help.  I will do my best to provide a helpful and accurate response.  Please let me know if there is anything",
