      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! Could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik": "Could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For handlebars, I would recommend considering a design that allows for a comfortable riding position and easy control. For a mountain bike used on forest trails and rough bike paths, a handlebar with a slight rise and a width that allows for a comfortable grip is a good choice. This type of handlebar can help reduce strain on your back and neck, and provide better control over the bike. Additionally, a handlebar with a bit of flex can help absorb shock and vibrations from the road, making for a more comfortable ride. Some popular types of handlebars for mountain biking include riser bars, flat bars, and drop bars. It's also a good idea to consider the material and durability of the handlebar, as well as any additional features such as grips or bar ends.  Please let me know if you need any further clarification.  Thank you.  I will be happy to answer any follow-up questions.  Please go ahead and ask your next question.  I am here to help",
          "citations": {},
