        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Clipless pedals can be a good option for mountain biking, especially if you're looking for a more efficient and secure connection to the bike. They can provide a more direct power transfer and better control, especially on technical terrain. However, they may require some practice to get used to, and can be more expensive than other types of pedals. Additionally, if you're planning to ride on rough or slippery surfaces, you may want to consider a pedal with a good grip, such as a platform pedal. Ultimately, the choice between clipless and platform pedals will depend on your personal preference and riding style.  Please let me know if you need any further clarification.  Thank you.  I will be happy to answer any follow-up questions.  Please go ahead and ask your next question.  I am here to help.  I will do my best to provide a helpful and accurate response.  Please let me know if there is anything else I can assist you with.  I am here to",
