      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks! Speaking of the seat\u2014what types of saddles work best for a mountain bike if most rides are on forest trails and rough paths?",
          "user_rubrik": "What types of saddles are recommended for a mountain bike used primarily on forest trails and rough bike paths?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For mountain biking on forest trails and rough paths, prioritize saddles designed for MTB that offer significant comfort. Look for features like orthopedic comfort foam padding, pressure-relieving cut-outs, and active technology that allows the saddle to flex with your pedaling. While comfort is key, avoid overly soft or wobbly saddles; a slightly firm, well-padded MTB-specific saddle like the SQlab 611 Ergowave Active S-Tube, Ergon SM, or WTB Rocket can provide both comfort and necessary support for varied terrain. Endurance saddles are also a good option for frequent trail riders.",
