        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Makes sense! Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Clipless pedals can offer better power transfer and stability on rough terrain, potentially aiding back pain by reducing bounce and improving control. Mountain bike specific clipless (2-bolt) systems are also designed for easier walking. However, they require practice to clip in and out quickly, and some sources suggest they're less suited for very challenging off-road trails, favoring smoother rides. Given your casual riding and comfort preference, while they offer efficiency, flat pedals might still provide more immediate ease and flexibility for your forest trails and rough paths.",
