      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense, thank you! Could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik": "Could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For your mountain bike, considering your back pain and preference for comfort, **riser handlebars** are highly recommended. They promote a more upright riding posture, which can alleviate strain on your back, and help distribute less weight to your hands and the front of the bike.\n\nLook for features like:\n*   **Adequate Rise**: Riser bars lift your hands to a higher, more comfortable position. Higher rise can shift more weight rearward, beneficial for comfort.\n*   **Proper Sweep**: Ensure the bar has the right sweep (angle) to position your wrists naturally and comfortably.\n*   **Material**: Both aluminum and carbon fiber are common, with carbon potentially offering more flex for comfort.\n\nPrioritize overall rider comfort when choosing.",
