        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm curious what parts I should check and maybe upgrade first on a second-hand bike. What would you prioritize?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the most important parts to inspect and upgrade first on a second-hand bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For your second-hand bike, prioritize checking and potentially upgrading the **brakes** (especially disc brakes for safety and varied conditions), **tires** (wider, durable ones for rough paths and stability), and **gear system** for hill climbing. For comfort, consider a **padded saddle** with shock absorption (like gel/foam or dual springs) and checking for **suspension** (fork or seat post) or **adjustable handlebars/grips** to absorb vibrations. These upgrades significantly enhance comfort and performance without requiring extensive DIY.",
