        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s clear! What types of saddles work best, especially for a mountain bike used on rough forest trails?",
          "user_rubrik": "What types of saddles are recommended for a mountain bike used primarily on forest trails and rough bike paths?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For mountain biking on rough forest trails, prioritize saddles with ample padding for comfort and shock absorption, like those with orthopedic foam or gel. While thick padding is good, avoid overly soft saddles that can become unsteady. Examples of comfortable MTB saddles include the WTB Rocket, Ergon SM, Selle Italia Diva Gel Superflow, and SQlab 611 Ergowave Active. Brooks leather saddles are generally not recommended for bumpy trail use due to insufficient padding. Synthetic materials are a popular, durable, and waterproof choice for MTB and casual riding.",
