      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great tips! Should I look for a particular saddle width or shape if I deal with lower back pain sometimes?",
          "user_rubrik": "Considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For lower back pain on rough trails, saddle width is crucial. A saddle that's too narrow won't support your sit bones, leading to hip and lower back strain. Get your sit bones measured at a bike shop to find the right width (e.g., 130-155mm range).\n\nLook for saddles with a broad, supportive shape, like those with raised wings, which can improve pressure distribution and posture. Specific designs, such as SQlab Ergowave with Active technology, are engineered to support natural pelvic movement and prevent lumbar spine pain. A suspension seat post can also significantly reduce impact on your back.",
