      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That helps a lot\u2014thanks! Could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik": "Could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a second-hand mountain bike used on rough forest trails and hills, especially with lower back pain, **riser bars** are generally recommended. They promote a more upright riding position, which can significantly reduce strain on your back and wrists.\n\nLook for handlebars with a comfortable sweep and rise that suits your body. Some carbon fiber mountain bike handlebars, like the RaceFace Atlas or Funn Black Ace, are specifically designed to absorb vibrations from rough terrain, enhancing comfort. Handlebars offering multiple hand positions, such as butterfly bars, can also help reduce fatigue on longer rides.",
