        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike for mostly forest trails and hills?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are clipless pedals worth considering on a mountain bike?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, clipless pedals are highly recommended for mountain biking on forest trails and hills, especially if you're looking to improve pedaling efficiency and power transfer. They ensure your foot stays connected throughout the entire pedal stroke, making climbing less strenuous and enhancing control on technical terrain. While there's a learning curve, the benefits for serious trail riding are significant. For mountain biking, two-bolt systems like Shimano SPD are most common due to their double-sided entry and mud-shedding design.",
