      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense, thanks! About the saddle\u2014what types are actually recommended for a mountain bike that\u2019s used mainly on forest trails and rough bike paths? I\u2019m all about comfort, not speed.",
          "user_rubrik": "What types of saddles are recommended for a mountain bike used primarily on forest trails and rough bike paths?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For comfort on your mountain bike, especially on forest trails and rough paths, prioritize saddles with ample padding for your sit bones. Mountain bike saddles typically have more padding than road saddles to absorb bumps. Look for features like pressure-relieving channels and durable covers.\n\nSaddles designed for recreational cycling often feature generous padding, gel, or even springs, which can be beneficial for casual rides. Specific options known for comfort on trails include the SQlab 611 Ergowave Active S-Tube Saddle, which flexes for comfort, and the Brooks C15 Saddle, noted for its suspension on rough terrain.",
