      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s helpful! Considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats?",
          "user_rubrik": "Considering my history of back pain, are there any important features to consider regarding bicycle seats? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For back pain on a mountain bike, prioritize seats with ample, thick padding like memory foam or gel to cushion impacts from rough trails. Look for shock-absorbing features such as dual springs or elastomer suspensions to protect your spine. An extra-wide, ergonomic design that distributes pressure evenly and includes pressure-relieving channels or cutouts is crucial for comfort and avoiding lower back strain. Additionally, ensure your seat height and angle are properly adjusted, as even small changes can significantly impact back comfort. A professional bike fitting can optimize your setup.",
