        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great tips! I\u2019ll check those out. Could you tell me a bit about handlebars for casual riding and bumpy city hills?",
          "user_rubrik": "Could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For casual riding on bumpy city hills, especially with a history of back pain, prioritize handlebars that promote an upright posture and absorb shock. Look for \"alt bars\" or \"comfort mountain bike bars\" with significant backsweep (15\u00b0 or more) and rise. This design helps reduce strain on your back by allowing you to sit more upright and positions your wrists comfortably. Riser handlebars are particularly beneficial as they bring you higher, improving comfort on varied terrain. Mountain bikes are well-suited for city riding and handling bumps.",
