      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice tips! Speaking of handlebars\u2014could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik": "Could you tell me about handlebars?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For mountain biking on forest trails and rough paths, prioritizing comfort and back pain, **riser handlebars** are highly recommended. They promote a more **upright posture**, which can significantly reduce strain on your back by shifting your weight rearward and taking pressure off your hands.\n\nLook for handlebars with:\n*   **Increased rise**: To achieve a higher, more relaxed hand position.\n*   **More backsweep or upsweep**: To ensure a neutral wrist position and absorb vibrations from rough terrain.\n*   **Wider designs**: For enhanced stability and comfort on challenging trails.\n\nThese \"comfort MTB\" or \"alt bars\" are specifically designed for long-distance comfort on varied terrain, aligning with your preference for comfort over speed.",
          "citations": {
